<div class="graphics-article-title" >
  FW20 Corduroy Styles
</div>
<div class="centered-article-text" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <p>
     There are a few different origin stories associated with Corduroy fabric. The first being that the word corduroy itself came from “cord du roi” or cord of the king. This folk etymology has been proven false and it is now believed that the word comes from a mix of the words “cord” and “duroy”. “Cord“ being the row-like texture or pattern found on the fabric and “duroy“ being adurable woolen cloth made in England throughout the 18th century and worn by factory workers in Manchester during the same time period.
  </p> 
</div>

